spec:
  grid: 15x15, background 0 [observed]
  gap_columns:
    count: exactly 2, each at col 1-13 (must be interior), separated by 4-8 cols
    gaps_per_column: 1-3, equal for both columns
  bars:
    layout: |
      Each gap column has N gap entries (rows). The bottom-most gap row is shared
      by both columns (a full-width bar with 2 gaps). The remaining N-1 entries per
      column are half-width bars that alternate left/right by row order.
    left_bars: span col 0 through some col strictly between c1 and c2 (gap at c1)
    right_bars: span some col strictly between c1 and c2 through col W-1 (gap at c2)
    full_bar: bottom-most row, spans full width with gaps at both c1 and c2; may have 1 or 2 colors (2 segments meeting adjacently, or single color)
    color: each bar segment has a unique non-bg color; within each column, the sequence of bar colors + terminal color has no repeats
    width: >=3 per segment (at least 1 cell on each side of gap) [observed min 5]
  terminal_markers:
    per_column: one vertical stripe of a single non-bg color below the last gap row, contiguous, touching the bottom edge
    length: 1-6 cells; gap of 0-2 empty rows between last bar and first marker cell
    color: unique within that column's sequence (bar colors + terminal)
  row_spacing: bars on distinct rows, spacing >=1 between consecutive bar rows
  total_colors: 3-7 distinct non-bg colors; colors may be shared across columns
  transform: |
    For each gap column, fill the entire column top-to-bottom: paint rows 0 through
    gap_row_k with bar_k's color (each segment from previous gap+1 to current gap),
    then paint remaining rows with the terminal color. Rest of grid unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 15x15, two gap column positions c1 < c2 with c2-c1 in 4-8 and both in 1-13
    2. Pick N = 1-3 (gaps per column). Choose 2*N + 2 distinct non-bg colors (N-1 left bars, N-1 right bars, 2 for full-width bottom bar halves, 2 terminals); colors may merge where allowed
    3. Build the output column fills first: for each gap column, assign N bar colors + 1 terminal color, partition rows 0..14 into N+1 contiguous segments, assign colors top-down
    4. Place the bottom shared bar row (last segment boundary of both columns); then interleave N-1 left-only and N-1 right-only bar rows above it, alternating sides
    5. For each bar row, draw horizontal bar cells spanning the appropriate range (left edge to mid-zone for left bars, mid-zone to right edge for right bars, full width for bottom bar), leaving the gap column cell empty
    6. Place terminal markers: for each gap column, place a contiguous vertical stripe of terminal color from some row below the last bar down to the bottom edge (1-6 cells, 0-2 empty row gap)
    7. All other cells are background; verify gap detection produces the intended gaps
